ght:12.7pt'>\r\n  <td width=354 valign=top style='width:265.5pt;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\r\n  height:12.7pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal style='line-height:115%'><b><span lang=EN-US\r\n  style='font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>Anti ds DNA (Anti Double\r\n  Stranded-DNA), Serum<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal style='line-height:115%'><span style='font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>(ECLIA)<\/span><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n  <td width=90 valign=top style='width:67.5pt;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\r\n  height:12.7pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal align=center style='text-align:center;line-height:115%'><b><span\r\n  lang=EN-US style='font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>10.6<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n  <td width=66 valign=top style='width:49.5pt;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\r\n  height:12.7pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal align=center style='text-align:center;line-height:115%'><span\r\n  lang=EN-US style='font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>IU\/mL<\/span><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n  <td width=192 valign=top style='width:144.0pt;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\r\n  height:12.7pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\n  style='font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&lt; 25.0 (Negative)<\/span><\/p>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\n  style='font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>25 - 30 (Borderline)<\/span><\/p>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\n  style='font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>31 - 60 (Low Positive)<\/span><\/p>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\n  style='font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>61 - 200 (Positive)<\/span><\/p>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal style='line-height:115%'><span lang=EN-US\r\n  style='font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&gt; 200 (Strong Positive)<\/span><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n <\/tr>\r\n <tr style='height:26.1pt'>\r\n  <td width=354 valign=top style='width:265.5pt;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\r\n  height:26.1pt'><\/td>\r\n  <td width=90 valign=top style='width:67.5pt;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\r\n  height:26.1pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal align=center style='text-align:center;line-height:115%'><span\r\n  lang=EN-US style='font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n  <td width=66 valign=top style='width:49.5pt;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\r\n  height:26.1pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal align=center style='text-align:center;line-height:115%'><span\r\n  lang=EN-US style='font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n  <td width=192 valign=top style='width:144.0pt;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\r\n  height:26.1pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal align=center style='text-align:center;line-height:115%'><span\r\n  lang=EN-US style='font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n <\/tr>\r\n<\/table>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:8.0pt;font-family:\"Arial\",sans-serif'>Interpretation:<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:8.0pt;font-family:\"Arial\",sans-serif'>===========<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:8.0pt;font-family:\"Arial\",sans-serif'>The anti-double stranded\r\nDNA (anti-dsDNA) test is used to help diagnose lupus (systemic lupus\r\nerythematosus, SLE) in<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:8.0pt;font-family:\"Arial\",sans-serif'>a person who has a\r\npositive result on a test for antinuclear antibody (ANA) and has clinical signs\r\nand symptoms that suggest lupus.<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:8.0pt'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:8.0pt'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:8.0pt;font-family:\"Arial\",sans-serif'>Anti-dsDNA is one of a\r\ngroup of autoantibodies called antinuclear antibodies that are produced by a\r\nperson's immune<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:8.0pt;font-family:\"Arial\",sans-serif'>system when it fails to\r\ndistinguish between &quot;self&quot; and &quot;nonself.&quot; ANA target\r\nsubstances found in the nucleus of cells.<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:8.0pt;font-family:\"Arial\",sans-serif'>Anti-dsDNA specifically\r\ntarget the genetic material (DNA) found in the nucleus, causing organ and\r\ntissue damage.<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:8.0pt;font-family:\"Arial\",sans-serif'>The presence of\r\nanti-dsDNA in the blood is strongly associated with the autoimmune disorder\r\nlupus.<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:8.0pt;font-family:\"Arial\",sans-serif'>The results of an\r\nanti-dsDNA test are usually considered together with a person's medical\r\nhistory, signs and symptoms,<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:8.0pt;font-family:\"Arial\",sans-serif'>and results of other\r\nautoantibody tests.<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:8.0pt;font-family:\"Arial\",sans-serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:8.0pt;font-family:\"Arial\",sans-serif'>A high level of\r\nanti-dsDNA in the blood is strongly associated with lupus and is often\r\nsignificantly increased during or<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:8.0pt;font-family:\"Arial\",sans-serif'>just prior to a\r\nflare-up. When the anti-dsDNA is positive and the person tested has other\r\nclinical signs and symptoms<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:8.0pt;font-family:\"Arial\",sans-serif'>associated with lupus,\r\nit means that the person tested likely has lupus. This is especially true if an\r\nanti-Sm test is also<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:8.0pt;font-family:\"Arial\",sans-serif'>positive.<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:8.0pt;font-family:\"Arial\",sans-serif'>In the evaluation of\r\nsomeone with lupus nephritis, a high level (titer) of anti-dsDNA is generally\r\nassociated with ongoing<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:8.0pt;font-family:\"Arial\",sans-serif'>inflammation and damage\r\nto the kidneys.<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:8.0pt;font-family:\"Arial\",sans-serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:8.0pt;font-family:\"Arial\",sans-serif'>A very low level of\r\nanti-dsDNA is considered negative but does not exclude a diagnosis of lupus.\r\nOnly about 50-70% of<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:8.0pt;font-family:\"Arial\",sans-serif'>those with lupus will\r\nhave anti-dsDNA.<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:8.0pt;font-family:\"Arial\",sans-serif'>Low to moderate levels\r\nof the autoantibody may be seen with other autoimmune disorders, such as\r\nSj\u00f6gren syndrome<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:8.0pt;font-family:\"Arial\",sans-serif'>and mixed connective\r\ntissue disease (MCTD).<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:8.0pt'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><b><span lang=EN-US>&nbsp;<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><b><span lang=EN-US>&nbsp;<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><b><span lang=EN-US>&nbsp;<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><b><span lang=EN-US>&nbsp;<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><b><span lang=EN-US>&nbsp;<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><b><span lang=EN-US>&nbsp;<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><b><span lang=EN-US>&nbsp;<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><b><span lang=EN-US>&nbsp;<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><b><span lang=EN-US>&nbsp;<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><b><span lang=EN-US>&nbsp;<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><b><span lang=EN-US>&nbsp;<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><b><span lang=EN-US>&nbsp;<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><b><span lang=EN-US>&nbsp;<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><b><span lang=EN-US>&nbsp;<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><b><span lang=EN-US>&nbsp;<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><b><span lang=EN-US>&nbsp;<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><b><span lang=EN-US>&nbsp;<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><b><span lang=EN-US>&nbsp;<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span style='position:relative;z-index:251657216;left:-52px;\r\ntop:259px;width:994px;height:261px'><img width=795 height=2\r\nsrc=\"data:image\/gif;base64,R0lGODlh4gMCAHcAMSH+GlNvZnR3YXJlOiBNaWNyb3NvZnQgT2ZmaWNlACH5BAEAAAAALAAAAADiAwIAgAAAAAAAAAJUhI+py+0Po5y02ouz3rz7D4biSJbmiabqyrbuC